College ERP - API Credentials & Integration Guide
Overview: This document details the backend environment variables, API base URLs, CORS configurations, and the primary integration points for the College ERP MERN stack application.
1. Deployment & Base URLs
The application is split between a React frontend and a Node.js/Express backend.

Frontend (Client) URL: https://erp-cell-one.vercel.app (Hosted on Vercel)
Backend (API) URL: https://erp-cell-nlh0.onrender.com (Hosted on Render)
Local Backend URL: http://localhost:5000/api
Local Frontend URL: http://localhost:5173
2. Environment Variables (.env Configuration)
The backend requires specific environment variables to connect to the database and sign authentication tokens.

PORT=5000
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://ionodecloud_db_user:ionodecloud_db_123@ionode.ckcssnb.mongodb.net/college-erp
JWT_SECRET=8da8e7db20a6197d6738a5a695eb561e33ad4e2d7e43a7ac744b63a84dde9034844e0410dcf35f03524cecfe34976f38524e3107d93a34e25841380f3617771f
JWT_EXPIRE=7d
NODE_ENV=development
3. CORS Configuration
The server is explicitly configured to only accept requests from the deployed frontend and local development environments to ensure security.

origin: [
    'https://erp-cell-one.vercel.app',
    'http://localhost:5173'
]
credentials: true
4. Frontend API Integration (Axios)
The React frontend utilizes Axios to communicate with the backend. It automatically switches between local and production URLs depending on the environment mode.

import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
    baseURL: import.meta.env.MODE === 'development'
        ? 'http://localhost:5000/api'
        : 'https://erp-cell-nlh0.onrender.com/api',
});

// Request Interceptor to attach JWT token for secure routes
api.interceptors.request.use((config) => {
    const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
    if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
    return config;
});

export default api;
5. API Route Structure
The backend logic is modularized into dedicated route files. Below are the primary integration endpoints for the frontend:

Auth: /api/auth (Handles Admin, Teacher, and Student logins, generating JWTs.)
Students: /api/students (CRUD operations for student records and credential generation.)
Teachers: /api/teachers (CRUD operations for teacher records.)
Branches: /api/branches (CRUD operations for academic departments.)
Fees: /api/fees (Fee structures and payment status updates.)
Attendance: /api/attendance (Logging, updating, and fetching class attendance records.)
Marks: /api/marks (Student grade tracking and evaluation.)